.TH HOMESTATE 1
.SH NAME
homestate \\- index and safely repair a home-directory state map
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homestate
homestate [--map-dir DIRECTORY] [--state FILE] [--index|--check|--new-files|--moved-files]
.br
[--broken-file-names|--fix-names|--restore-names]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Indexes a directory, reports changes and moves, and can apply reversible filename repairs using its recorded mapping.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBhomestate --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
